; level map for our mario game
; 60 columns x 12 rows = 720 bytes, one byte per tile
; to find a tile: row*60 + column (getTile does this)
; row 0 is kept empty for the HUD, rows 10 and 11 are the ground

; tile numbers (double check with Subhan's constants.inc):
; 0 empty, 1 ground, 2 brick, 3 coin ? block, 4 mushroom ? block
; 6 7 =pipe top (left, right), 8 9 = pipe body (left, right)
; 10 =stair block, 11 =coin, 12 =flag pole

; things in the level (columns start from 0):
; two pits at columns 14-16 and 38-40 (no ground, mario falls)
; 2 tile high pipe at columns 20-21, 3 tile high pipe at columns 33-34
; two brick groups of 3 bricks, at columns 23-25 and 44-46
; stairs go up 4 steps (columns 52-55), flag pole is 7 tiles tall at column 57

